  "live_records": {
    "q-38864": {
      "dom_id": "step-q38864",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\,$ $T({b}_{1})=2{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1},\\,$ $T({b}_{2})=4{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{3})=7{c}_{2}-5{c}_{1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write the images of vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})=2{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2})=4{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{3})=7{c}_{2}-5{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2})$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
