    "q-140426": {
      "dom_id": "step-q140426",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\,$ $T({b}_{1})=6{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}-7{c}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=-5{c}_{2}+9{c}_{3}-4{c}_{1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write the images of vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})=6{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}-7{c}_{3} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2})=-5{c}_{2}+9{c}_{3}-4{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and  $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -5 \\\\ -7 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-140426-a",
