    "q-97577": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97577",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 27 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-97577-a",
