    "q-97587": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97587",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -7 & 6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
