      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Image of a Vector Given With Respect to the Standard Basis Under a Linear Map",
      "kp_id": "e-5522"
    },
    "q-97588": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97588",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
